/* Base-language purpose strings.

   These duplicate the INFOPLIST_KEY_* values in project.yml on purpose: those settings are
   what a reviewer reads next to the entitlements, and this file is what the system actually
   shows once the app has more than one localisation. iOS prefers the localised value, so a
   change to one has to be made in both — a drift here means a user sees the wording of a
   language they did not pick.

   Wording is bound by .claude/skills/appstore_compliance/SKILL.md: tracking and personal
   patterns only. */

"NSMotionUsageDescription" = "Barosense reads barometric pressure to track weather changes alongside your check-ins.";

"NSHealthShareUsageDescription" = "Barosense reads your sleep, resting heart rate and blood oxygen to look for personal patterns between weather and how you feel. It stays on your device.";

"NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription" = "Barosense uses your location to fetch the local pressure forecast.";
